# SCSS Module Best Practices

When working with SCSS modules:

- Always use `@use` instead of `@import` for importing SCSS modules
- Place `@use` statements before any other statements, including `@import url()`
- Use namespaces when importing modules: `@use '../styles/variables.scss' as vars;`
- Reference variables and mixins using namespace: `vars.$variable-name` and `@include vars.mixin-name`
- Never use global variables without namespace
- Do not use the `prependData` option in Next.js config for SCSS imports

## Example of correct SCSS usage

```scss
@use '../styles/variables.scss' as vars;
@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Press+Start+2P&display=swap');

.myClass {
  color: vars.$text-primary;
  font-size: vars.$base-font-size;
  @include vars.pixel-text;
}
```
